Silo patch 0028 — setupapi base containerid wchar (DualSense, from MacGameFix)

Origin: MacGameFix (https://github.com/MathiasKowoll/MacGameFix) engine/patches/wine-11.0/0010-setupapi-base-containerid-wchar.patch (Mathias Kowoll,
LGPL-2.1-or-later, the Wine modules' license; MacGameFix at da9c470, 2026-11-25). Code unchanged. MacGameFix's series
0001-0016 is Silo's 0019-0034, in the same order; 0035 moves its settings and logs into Silo's own folders.

What it does (setupapi.dll), as MacGameFix's engine/README.md says:
  SetupDiGetDeviceRegistryPropertyA returns SPDRP_BASE_CONTAINERID as the W function does, a WCHAR string, as
  Windows returns it.

Checked here: the whole series applies after 0002-0018 with no fuzz; built with the runtime's flags and played on
2026-11-26 with a DualSense over Bluetooth, Steam Input off, from Steam for macOS: UNCHARTED (input, trigger effects,
rumble on the actuators) and The Last of Us Part II.

--- a/dlls/setupapi/devinst.c
+++ b/dlls/setupapi/devinst.c
@@ -3467,6 +3467,14 @@
         SetLastError(ERROR_INVALID_DATA);
         return FALSE;
     }
+
+    /* Windows returns the base container id as a WCHAR string from the ANSI function as well
+     * (the ntoskrnl tests read it with the W one for that reason). A game that reads a pad's
+     * container with one and an audio endpoint's with the other compares two WCHAR strings;
+     * Nioh 3 does, and never finds the pad's output when this one is ANSI. */
+    if (Property == SPDRP_BASE_CONTAINERID)
+        return SetupDiGetDeviceRegistryPropertyW(devinfo, device_data, Property, PropertyRegDataType,
+                PropertyBuffer, PropertyBufferSize, RequiredSize);
 
     if (Property < ARRAY_SIZE(PropertyMap) && PropertyMap[Property].nameA)
     {
